{"lines": [{"text": "Twenty years ago, a hundred dollars filled this cart.", "start": 0.5, "end": 3.596, "spec": null, "words": [["Twenty", 0.091, 0.307], ["years", 0.307, 0.523], ["ago", 0.523, 0.909], ["a", 1.114, 1.159], ["hundred", 1.216, 1.568], ["dollars", 1.568, 1.943], ["filled", 1.955, 2.273], ["this", 2.273, 2.42], ["cart", 2.432, 2.773]]}, {"text": "Today, the same cart costs roughly one hundred seventy dollars.", "start": 4.4, "end": 8.312, "spec": null, "words": [["Today", 0.091, 0.398], ["the", 0.602, 0.705], ["same", 0.716, 0.977], ["cart", 0.977, 1.25], ["costs", 1.261, 1.648], ["roughly", 1.75, 2.227], ["one", 2.318, 2.511], ["hundred", 2.511, 2.75], ["seventy", 2.75, 3.068], ["dollars", 3.068, 3.58]]}, {"text": "That slow, steady rise in prices is called inflation.", "start": 8.612, "end": 11.972, "spec": null, "words": [["That", 0.091, 0.182], ["slow", 0.182, 0.682], ["steady", 1.08, 1.341], ["rise", 1.341, 1.625], ["in", 1.625, 1.716], ["prices", 1.716, 2.148], ["is", 2.148, 2.227], ["called", 2.227, 2.443], ["inflation", 2.455, 3.023]]}, {"text": "Statisticians track it with a basket of thousands of everyday prices, from rent and food to fuel and haircuts.", "start": 12.272, "end": 19.4, "spec": null, "words": [["Statisticians", 0.091, 0.75], ["track", 0.75, 1.125], ["it", 1.125, 1.284], ["with", 1.409, 1.534], ["a", 1.534, 1.58], ["basket", 1.591, 2.08], ["of", 2.08, 2.148], ["thousands", 2.148, 2.75], ["of", 2.761, 2.852], ["everyday", 2.989, 3.364], ["prices", 3.364, 3.977], ["from", 4.193, 4.443], ["rent", 4.443, 4.727], ["and", 4.875, 4.989], ["food", 4.989, 5.489], ["to", 5.705, 5.795], ["fuel", 5.795, 6.114], ["and", 6.114, 6.17], ["haircuts", 6.17, 6.795]]}, {"text": "Prices usually climb for three simple reasons.", "start": 19.7, "end": 23.084, "spec": null, "words": [["Prices", 0.091, 0.523], ["usually", 0.523, 0.886], ["climb", 0.898, 1.364], ["for", 1.534, 1.705], ["three", 1.705, 2.193], ["simple", 2.193, 2.511], ["reasons", 2.511, 3.045]]}, {"text": "First, when people want to buy more than shops can supply, sellers can raise prices.", "start": 23.384, "end": 28.232, "spec": null, "words": [["First", 0.125, 0.568], ["when", 0.795, 0.898], ["people", 0.898, 1.159], ["want", 1.159, 1.273], ["to", 1.273, 1.33], ["buy", 1.33, 1.432], ["more", 1.432, 1.716], ["than", 1.727, 1.807], ["shops", 1.818, 2.159], ["can", 2.17, 2.273], ["supply", 2.273, 2.807], ["sellers", 3.193, 3.557], ["can", 3.557, 3.67], ["raise", 3.67, 3.864], ["prices", 3.875, 4.511]]}, {"text": "Second, when energy, materials or wages get more expensive, businesses pass part of that on.", "start": 28.532, "end": 35.036, "spec": null, "words": [["Second", 0.091, 0.58], ["when", 0.818, 0.977], ["energy", 1.034, 1.568], ["materials", 1.807, 2.466], ["or", 2.523, 2.693], ["wages", 2.693, 3.318], ["get", 3.409, 3.568], ["more", 3.58, 3.807], ["expensive", 3.807, 4.5], ["businesses", 4.761, 5.205], ["pass", 5.205, 5.58], ["part", 5.591, 5.773], ["of", 5.773, 5.807], ["that", 5.807, 5.966], ["on", 5.966, 6.182]]}, {"text": "Third, when money and credit grow faster than the goods they chase, each dollar is worth a little less.", "start": 35.336, "end": 41.456, "spec": null, "words": [["Third", 0.125, 0.557], ["when", 0.795, 0.989], ["money", 0.989, 1.33], ["and", 1.341, 1.443], ["credit", 1.455, 1.864], ["grow", 1.966, 2.261], ["faster", 2.261, 2.727], ["than", 2.727, 2.807], ["the", 2.807, 2.875], ["goods", 2.875, 3.114], ["they", 3.125, 3.239], ["chase", 3.239, 3.716], ["each", 4.159, 4.341], ["dollar", 4.352, 4.705], ["is", 4.705, 4.795], ["worth", 4.795, 5.034], ["a", 5.045, 5.08], ["little", 5.08, 5.307], ["less", 5.318, 5.795]]}, {"text": "That's why many central banks, like the Fed and the European Central Bank, aim for about two percent a year.", "start": 41.756, "end": 47.636, "spec": null, "words": [["That's", 0.102, 0.205], ["why", 0.205, 0.33], ["many", 0.33, 0.602], ["central", 0.602, 0.92], ["banks", 0.932, 1.432], ["like", 1.568, 1.693], ["the", 1.705, 1.773], ["Fed", 1.784, 2.261], ["and", 2.409, 2.477], ["the", 2.477, 2.511], ["European", 2.511, 2.966], ["Central", 2.977, 3.261], ["Bank", 3.273, 3.614], ["aim", 4.034, 4.216], ["for", 4.227, 4.398], ["about", 4.398, 4.636], ["two", 4.636, 4.807], ["percent", 4.818, 5.136], ["a", 5.148, 5.159], ["year", 5.159, 5.557]]}, {"text": "Small and steady, so people can plan, save and borrow without nasty surprises.", "start": 47.936, "end": 53.12, "spec": null, "words": [["Small", 0.091, 0.523], ["and", 0.534, 0.614], ["steady", 0.614, 1.068], ["so", 1.432, 1.591], ["people", 1.591, 1.852], ["can", 1.852, 1.943], ["plan", 1.943, 2.352], ["save", 2.705, 3.011], ["and", 3.023, 3.102], ["borrow", 3.114, 3.466], ["without", 3.477, 3.852], ["nasty", 3.852, 4.17], ["surprises", 4.17, 4.83]]}, {"text": "But two percent adds up: after ten years, prices are about twenty percent higher.", "start": 53.42, "end": 58.436, "spec": null, "words": [["But", 0.102, 0.193], ["two", 0.193, 0.364], ["percent", 0.364, 0.807], ["adds", 0.932, 1.205], ["up", 1.216, 1.432], ["after", 1.886, 2.136], ["ten", 2.136, 2.375], ["years", 2.375, 2.83], ["prices", 2.955, 3.375], ["are", 3.386, 3.455], ["about", 3.455, 3.67], ["twenty", 3.67, 3.977], ["percent", 3.977, 4.341], ["higher", 4.341, 4.693]]}, {"text": "After twenty years, the same dollar buys roughly a third less.", "start": 58.736, "end": 62.864, "spec": null, "words": [["After", 0.091, 0.307], ["twenty", 0.307, 0.545], ["years", 0.545, 1.011], ["the", 1.205, 1.307], ["same", 1.307, 1.568], ["dollar", 1.568, 1.841], ["buys", 1.852, 2.25], ["roughly", 2.261, 2.693], ["a", 2.807, 2.841], ["third", 2.852, 3.261], ["less", 3.261, 3.795]]}, {"text": "That's why cash in a drawer quietly loses value, even though the number on the bill never changes.", "start": 63.164, "end": 68.732, "spec": null, "words": [["That's", 0.091, 0.239], ["why", 0.239, 0.398], ["cash", 0.398, 0.841], ["in", 0.852, 0.909], ["a", 0.909, 0.966], 